abstract: "Multiplying by a real number changes size by the factor |b| and keeps or flips direction according to its sign. This elementary organization explains the sign rule, inverses, why multiplication by zero cannot be undone, and when multiplying makes a number bigger. Teaching hypotheses are stated as untested. Prepared with AI assistance; not peer reviewed."
